limiting membrane flap technique versus pars plana vitrectomy with conventional internal limiting membrane peeling for  
treating large macular holes, including idiopathic, traumatic, and myopic macular holes.",                              
    "background": "Macular hole (MH) is a full‐thickness defect in the central portion of the retina that causes loss of
