These differences may be the basis for the underlying pathophysiologic factors contributing to the development of MH."},
{"study_index": 10, "title": "Inverted internal limiting membrane flap technique versus internal limiting membrane 
peeling for large macular holes: a meta-analysis of randomized controlled trials", "abstract": "BACKGROUND Vitrectomy 
with internal limiting membrane (ILM) peeling is an effective surgical procedure for the treatment of macular holes 
(MHs). However, there is a possibility of poor postoperative anatomical closure with conventional ILM peeling for MHs 
larger than 400 μm. Therefore, a novel inverted ILM flap technique was developed for such cases. OBJECTIVES This 
meta-analysis study was performed to evaluate and compare the anatomical and visual outcomes of the inverted ILM flap 
