### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
The screening was conservative, following the guideline to INCLUDE when uncertain. However, in this batch, the exclusion
criteria were clear for 19 studies. The only included study (Study 20) is a well-designed prospective RCT that directly 
addresses the review question. Studies 17 and 19 were RCTs but compared variations within the inverted ILM flap 
technique rather than comparing ILM peeling vs inverted ILM flap as required by the protocol. This highlights the 
importance of precise intervention comparison in systematic reviews.


